On the 18th of April 1943, four young boys discovered a skeleton buried in the hollow of a witch arm tree in Hagley Woods, in the Worcestershire County of England. Police immediately got to work on identifying the remains and trying to determine the cause of death. However, the investigation hit a wall pretty early on. There were no witnesses, no physical evidence, no suspects, no real leads at all. They couldn't even identify the remains. But about eight months later, the messages started to appear around town.
1943年4月18日，四个小男孩在英国伍斯特郡黑格利森林（Hagley Woods）的一棵魔女榆树（Witch elm）树洞里，发现了一具被埋葬的骨骼。警察立即着手查明遗骸身份并试图确定死因。然而，调查很早就陷入了僵局。没有目击证人，没有物证，没有嫌疑人，根本没有任何真正的线索。他们甚至无法辨认遗骸的身份。但在大约八个月后，小镇各处开始出现一些讯息。

